  - question: How many downspouts do I need?
    answer: "<p>Generally, one downspout per 20-30 linear feet of gutter. Larger roofs or heavy rainfall areas may need more. We'll assess your specific situation.</p>"
  - question: Can you extend my downspouts?
    answer: "<p>Absolutely. Extensions, splash blocks, and underground connections move water well away from your foundation.</p>"
  - question: What size downspouts are best?
    answer: "<p>Standard 2x3-inch works for most homes, but 3x4-inch handles more volume — often better for North Alabama's heavy rainfall.</p>"
  - question: My downspouts drain too close to my foundation. Can you fix this?
